---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: home
---
<section class="home-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted todo board</p>
  <h1>{{ site.tagline }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Projects hold todos, laid out as a board of lanes. Todos can depend on other
    todos, and one you are waiting on cannot be ticked off yet. Give a lane an
    agent and it works each todo that arrives there. One container plus
    Postgres, and AI is off until you switch it on.
  </p>
  <p class="cta">
    <a class="button" href="{{ '/get-started/' | url }}">Get started</a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="{{ site.repo }}" rel="noopener">View on GitHub ↗</a>
  </p>

  <div class="board" role="img" aria-label="A board with four lanes: Inbox, Build with a Worker agent, Review with a Reviewer agent, and Done.">
    <div class="lane">
      <div class="lane-head">Inbox</div>
      <div class="todo">Write the release notes<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip label">docs</span></span></div>
      <div class="todo blocked">Tag 2.1<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip">waits on 2</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lane">
      <div class="lane-head">Build <span class="lane-agent">Worker</span></div>
      <div class="todo">Add CSV export<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip running">running</span></span></div>
      <div class="todo">Fix the date picker<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip fail">sent back</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lane">
      <div class="lane-head">Review <span class="lane-agent">Reviewer</span></div>
      <div class="todo">Paginate the runs list<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip">attempt 1 of 3</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lane">
      <div class="lane-head">Done</div>
      <div class="todo done">Dark mode<span class="todo-marks"><span class="mark-chip pass">pass</span></span></div>
      <div class="todo done">Labels on projects</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🔗</div>
      <h3>Dependencies</h3>
      <p>A blocked todo sits in its own section with its blockers named and its checkbox disabled. Cycles are rejected when you try to make them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🗂️</div>
      <h3>A board, or a list</h3>
      <p>The same todos as lanes you name yourself, one of which means done. Drag a card there and it is ticked off. Labels attach to projects and todos alike.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🤖</div>
      <h3>Agents on lanes</h3>
      <p>An agent is a model and its instructions. Put one on a lane and each todo there becomes a run that passes or fails and follows the lane's route.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🔌</div>
      <h3>Your own tools, over MCP</h3>
      <p>Point Claude Code or any MCP client at <code>/mcp</code> with an API key. Each key has a switch per tool, so a read-only key is one with its writing tools off.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">🎚️</div>
      <h3>AI off until you want it</h3>
      <p>Switches on the instance, the account and the project, plus auto-run and "AI ignores this" on a todo. Set <code>AI_ENABLED=false</code> to remove it outright.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <div class="feature-icon">📦</div>
      <h3>One container plus Postgres</h3>
      <p>The app and the API share one origin, migrations run at boot, and sign-in is a magic link written to the log. Nothing to clone, nothing to build.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

